  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financial Inclusion Improves Sanitation and Health (FINISH)-Mondial 2021-2025 + bridging phase 2019-2020.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FINISH Mondial aims to scale up access and use of safely managed sanitation in six countries: Bangladesh, Ethiopia, India, Kenya, Tanzania and Uganda. In the period 2021-2025, FINISH aims to reach 5 million people with safely managed sanitation through the realization of 1 million safely managed sanitation systems. 
FINISH Mondial works via the &#x201C;diamond approach&#x201D;, bringing together and building capacity of communities, businesses, micro finance institutions and government and improving access to finance for sanitary facilities and business development. A key element of this approach is the focus on circular economy: this will increase sustainability through re-use of faecal sludge and organic waste (fertilizer or energy). Another important element is capacity building for micro finance institutions, to develop sanitation loan products, in order crowd in commercial finance in the sanitation sector.</narrative>
  </description>
